[Music]  hi  have you ever been in a situation where  you couldn't remember the word you  wanted  don't worry it happens to everyone even  native speakers and in a speaking exam  when you're maybe nervous and stressed  it can be even worse so here are four  things you can do to communicate when  you don't know or can't remember a word  in english  the first technique is to find a more  general word or explain the word for  example if you can't remember the word  surgeon you could say doctor or if you  can't remember the word kitten you could  say  baby cat  [Music]  describing the purpose of an item in a  sentence can also be useful if you don't  know the word scissors you could say  they are used to cut paper or they are  used for cutting paper this works best  for nouns  for nouns and adjectives you can use  synonyms synonyms are simply two words  that mean the same or have a very  similar meaning  for example clever is a synonym for  intelligent and stone is a synonym for  rock antonyms are opposite words you can  often describe an adjective using the  opposite adjective if you can't remember  the word old you could say  not young for example  one more technique to use when you can't  remember a word is approximations  you can say it's like a house or it's  kind of a house with only one floor when  you're trying to describe a bungalow  remember you can always use more than  one of these language techniques at once  so if you can't remember the word for an  office block you could say it's a kind  of tool building where people go to work  at desks  [Music]  for more tips on learning english and  preparing for your exam subscribe to our  channel and visit the learn english  teens website where you will find loads  more learning material to help you  improve your english  [Music]  you

